Hi all,

Please find below the external counsel’s opinion on the grounds of the appeal you proposed:

{color:#36b37e}Following to our call on Tuesday, please, find below, some heads up about appeal after having studied the documentation and started to work on the grounds:{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

* {color:#36b37e}The chances of success of the appeal are moderate in our view. By moderate, we mean that the arguments suggested in your working documents are not conclusive but some of them can be reasonably defended (others should, in our view, be dropped as explained below). From a more strategic perspective, even if the chances of success are moderate, an appeal might give the chance for the Administration to reconsidering the assessment of the more subjective criteria (essentially, 6 & 7).{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

* {color:#36b37e}Additionally, please note that the decision that we would be appealing does not only serve to grant the 3 authorizations but also establishes the order to be followed in the future to replace the winners in case any of them loses its authorization during the 3-year term. Therefore, the fact that Bolt would only raise to position 4 after the appeal might have some relevance as to further justify the appeal.  {color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

* {color:#36b37e}On the other hand, very briefly, we suggest concentrating our appeal on the following grounds you raised in your working documents:{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

# {color:#36b37e}*_The award process - As explained above, Madrid council did not follow the process and timelines as stated in the ITT and only the winning operators were notified about the award (screenshots of (i) the media posts prior to the official notification award and (ii) the inconsistencies regarding official award time are available)._*{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}ECIJA: We might need to reformulate a bit the argument. The ITT envisages separate notifications to the winners and to the losers. The ITT expressly envisages the possibility of not notifying to the loser the result of the process at all. Therefore, we would be focusing on the fact that the result of the valuation was first notified to the three companies that finally obtained the authorization instead to all the participants at the same time as requested in the ITT.{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

# {color:#36b37e}*_Requirement f) - Refers to the presentation of documentation accrediting the MAAS Platform in which it is integrated. Lime did not comply with the requirement as they presented a self-declaration committing to integrating with Madrid 360 platform._*{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}ECIJA: We would argue that self-declarations shall only be admissible as substitutes of documentation when expressly envisaged in the tender documentation (the ITT here). Admittedly, in response to some questions posed by the participants in connection with this, the Administration accepted here the self-declaration instead of the documentation required in the IIT. However, we would argue that the Administration cannot alter the content of the ITT by way of clarifications (i.e., it cannot be clarified what it is clear).{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

# {color:#36b37e}*_Criteria 6 and 7 - In the evaluation reports of the three winners, these criteria have been assessed by giving high importance/score to (i) aspects that we also accredited in our submission and which were not equally scored and(ii) also to solutions that do not fall within the scope/description/requirements of Criteria 6 and 7, such as collaborations with ONCE (organization for visually impaired people in Spain), drunk test features or investments in parking infrastructure. On the other hand, at least one of the winners seems to be overscored considering they provided a poor explanation regarding the management of their technical solutions/developments._*{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}ECIJA: We would argue that technical discretion does not justify subjective, arbitrary o discriminatory decisions. We would also argue that “improvements” (i.e., additional features not envisaged in the ITT) cannot be taken into consideration if they are not specified as a criterion in the ITT (as in this case). This is a principle of public procurement rules aimed at avoiding arbitrary decisions. Public procurement principles apply to this competitive process as clarified in the ITT.{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

* {color:#36b37e}By contrast, we should be dropping the following grounds:{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

# {color:#36b37e}*_Criteria 5_*{color}{color:#36b37e} _- Two operators, VOI and Dott, did not provide the sworn declaration required by the tender specifications and instead submitted an Integration certificate into the Madrid Mobility 360 Platform and nevertheless obtained the highest score for this criterion. If the Integration certificate was accepted by analogy by the City, this should have been described in the ITT._{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}ECIJA: It is a weak argument. Too formalistic. The certificate is a better source of evidence of the fulfillment of the criteria than the sworn declaration.   {color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

# {color:#36b37e}*_Criteria 8_*{color}{color:#36b37e} _-_{color}{color:#36b37e} {color}{color:#36b37e}_The action plan was scored evenly across all the operators except for two and apparently has not been through an assessment as thorough as Criteria 6 and 7. No breakdown has been given around how they scored / valued the criteria._{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}ECIJA: It is a weak argument, and, in addition, we are not sure that this would necessarily benefit BOLT (as BOLT got the highest possible score and the outcome of a reevaluation is uncertain).{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

# {color:#36b37e}*_Criteria 4 and 9_*{color}{color:#36b37e} _- Whilst the requirement was scored based on the decrease in the time of response when a badly parked scooter is reported and the number of safety training courses given to users, the Criteria also required to provide a justification on how these are achieved. There is no reference to this justification in the evaluation reports provided by the City Council._{color}

{color:#36b37e} {color}

{color:#36b37e}       ECIJA: As the Administration clarified, only the commitment of the companies to reach their proposed numbers is taken into consideration. Therefore, there is no need to provide justification.{color}



{color:#36b37e}If you have any questions or concerns or would like to have a short conversation today, please let us know. In the meantime, we are still working in the appeal to meet the Monday 27 deadline.{color}



