# having more balanced termination rights is important - the landlord has a right to immediate terminate the contract, Bolt should have it as well, in case e.g.
{color:#403294}The owner has a right o terminate the contract only if we’d damage the property or misuse it. I would put in a 14 days warning period for us to either fix the problem we’ve cause or to leave the premises. We also have a right to terminate the contract immediately, either by mutual agreement or if the owner isn’t able to provide us the required conditions for us (116/1990zb){color}

_Immediate termination events for Bolt to be added, e.g._

* _the Landlord commits a material breach of any term of this Agreement. -_ {color:#403294}_we have it covered above_{color}
* _the Premises cannot be used for Bolt’s intended activity due the reasons independent from Bolt. -_ {color:#403294}_we have it covered above_{color}
* _the continuous use (24 hours a day, 365 days a year) is denied or refused or frustrated by the landlord,_ {color:#403294}_- we have it covered above_{color}

2. Our insurance cannot cover/exclude the landlord’s liability in case of event caused by the landlord. 
{color:#403294}The owner in the contract is biding himself to keep the premises to be in an answering state that goes with our intended purpose. {color}
3. The purpose of the lease should be specified - i.e. maintenance, storage, charging of e-scooters and e-bikers, including litihum batteries.- 

{color:#403294}this could limit us in the future. The contract says that we landlord has to provide everything for us so we may be able to fulfill our business purpose (maintenance of the scooters, storing, etc.). If we would specify it in the contract, in the future we might have to reopen the contract because of a added business purpose (e-bikes, service centre, etc.){color}

4. The scope and costs coverage of the necessary repairs, improvements, etc. - this could possibly create the disputes in the future. - 

{color:#403294}in the contract we have specified the cost coverage. It there’s a damaged on the property not caused by us, the owner is responsible for fixing it. The owner as also right to improve his premises without our permission, only has to notify us. In this case it’s also covered by the owner and it can’t limit us by our work. {color}

Hopefully it cleared out some point. If there’s something else, just let me know.

